{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_58c548dd82749a7a453bea7b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to understand the existing tests to know exactly what's expected. Then implement the two functions and add tests.\n\nLet's look at the contracts again carefully.\n\nFor `summarizeAssistants(runs)`:\n1. Throw TypeError when runs is not an array. (message can be anything, just TypeError)\n2. A run is eligible when `status === \"complete\"`, `acceptance_status === \"pass\"`, and `comparison_eligible !== false`. So `comparison_eligible` can be true, undefined, or not present - all are eligible as long as it's not false.\n3. Validate eligible runs: `run_id` and `assistant` must be non-empty strings; `score` finite number 0-100; `elapsed_ms` finite number >= 0. Throw TypeError for invalid eligible data. Ineligible runs invalid fields don't matter.\n4. Group eligible runs by exact case-sensitive assistant value.\n5. Return one object per assistant with exactly these fields: assistant, run_count, best_score, best_run_id, median_elapsed_ms.\n6. Best run: highest score, tie break lower elapsed time, then lexicographically smaller run_id.\n7. Median: all eligible runs for assistant after numeric sort. Even count: average of two middle values.\n8. Sort returned summaries by assistant string comparison. Do not mutate input.\n\nFor `renderComparisonTable(summaries)`:\n1. Throw TypeError when summaries is not an array or a summary has invalid fields. `assistant` and `best_run_id` must be non-empty strings; `run_count` positive integer; `best_score` finite number 0-100; `median_elapsed_ms` finite number >= 0.\n2. Preserve supplied summary order.\n3. Exact Markdown header:\n   `| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |`\n   followed by:\n   `|---|---:|---:|---|---:|`\n4. Render median milliseconds as seconds with exactly three decimal places. e.g., 1250 -> 1.250 s\n5. Escape `|` in assistant names and run IDs as `\\|`.\n6. Empty array: header, blank line, `_No eligible runs._`.\n\nNow I need to check if there are any schemas or other fixtures to understand data types. Let me also look at directory structure.\n\nLet me read the schema files or task contract for any specifics.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":7135,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d","uuid":"b5fd30f1-c4aa-42e0-98d3-c6702c580fdc","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:09:04.350Z"}
