{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":3305,"estimated_tokens_delta":1,"uuid":"6446e08e-e004-4782-80df-08a5e3ca81ea","session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_4703e21c94d35de9d9920cff","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The run schema has assistant enum but in the fixtures tests use \"Codex\", \"Claude Code\", \"OpenCode\" - so the contract says exact case-sensitive value. We just use the value in the run. The validation is that it is a non-empty string.\n\nNow let's implement. I need to consider edge cases:\n\nFor summarizeAssistants:\n- Non-array -> TypeError\n- Eligible run validation: run_id non-empty string, assistant non-empty string, score finite 0-100, elapsed_ms finite >= 0\n- comparison_eligible !== false means true, undefined, absent are all eligible\n- Need to check \"complete\" and \"pass\"\n- Group by assistant\n- best run: highest score, lower elapsed, smaller run_id lexicographically\n- median: numeric sort; odd - middle; even - average of two middle\n- sort summaries by assistant\n- don't mutate input\n\nFor renderComparisonTable:\n- Non-array -> TypeError\n- Each summary must have exact required fields? Contract says \"or a summary has invalid fields\". It lists field requirements. It says \"summary has invalid fields\" - so we need to validate. But does it require checking no extra fields? The contract says \"exactly these fields\" for summarizeAssistants output, but for render input it just says fields must be valid. I think we don't need to reject extra properties, but we need required fields valid. Let me check tests. The test uses an object with those exact fields. Since the function is meant to be used with summarizeAssistants output, I think checking required fields and their types is sufficient. But to be safe, we could check exactly those fields. Hmm.\n\nActually, the contract says: \"Throw TypeError when summaries is not an array or a summary has invalid fields. assistant and best_run_id must be non-empty strings; run_count must be a positive integer; best_score must be a finite number from 0 through 100; and median_elapsed_ms must be a finite number greater than or equal to zero.\"\n\nThis doesn't explicitly say \"exactly these fields\" for render input. So I won't reject extra fields. But the summarize output has exactly those fields. I'll just validate the listed fields exist and are valid.\n\nWait, should I check that each summary is an object? Probably yes. If summary is not an object, accessing fields would fail. I'll throw TypeError.\n\nFor median_elapsed_ms validation: finite number >= 0.\n\nFormatting seconds: (ms / 1000).toFixed(3) + \" s\". Need to be careful with toFixed rounding but that's standard.\n\nEdge cases for toFixed: 1.250 -> \"1.250\". 1250/1000 = 1.25 -> \"1.250\". Good.\n\nEmpty array: return header + \"\\n\" + separator + \"\\n\" + \"\" + \"\\n\" + \"_No eligible runs._\". So join with newlines as in test.\n\nNow let's write the code.\n\nFor median calculation:\nfunction median(values) {\n  const sorted = [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  const mid = Math.floor(sorted.length / 2);\n  if (sorted.length % 2 === 1) return sorted[mid];\n  return (sorted[mid - 1] + sorted[mid]) / 2;\n}\n\nBest run selection:\nfunction bestRun(runs) {\n  return runs.reduce((best, run) => {\n    if (run.score > best.score) return run;\n    if (run.score < best.score) return best;\n    if (run.elapsed_ms < best.elapsed_ms) return run;\n    if (run.elapsed_ms > best.elapsed_ms) return best;\n    return run.run_id < best.run_id ? run : best;\n  });\n}\n\nNow validation functions:\nfunction isNonEmptyString(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"string\" && value.length > 0;\n}\n\nfunction isFiniteNumber(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value);\n}\n\nFor score: isFiniteNumber(score) && score >= 0 && score <= 100\nFor elapsed_ms: isFiniteNumber(elapsed_ms) && elapsed_ms >= 0\n\nNow grouping. Use Map or object.\n\nEligible check:\nrun.status === \"complete\" && run.acceptance_status === \"pass\" && run.comparison_eligible !== false\n\nIf eligible, validate:\n- run_id non-empty string\n- assistant non-empty string\n- score finite 0-100\n- elapsed_ms finite >=0\n\nWhat about status and acceptance_status being strings? The contract says eligible only when those exact values. It doesn't say validate them. We just check equality.\n\nNow for the return: exactly fields. Since we create new objects, that's fine.\n\nSort by assistant: normal JS string comparison. Array.sort() uses string comparison by default for strings. But to be explicit, (a, b) => a.assistant.localeCompare(b.assistant)? Contract says \"normal JavaScript string comparison\". In JS, `<` and `>` for strings uses UTF-16 code units. localeCompare uses locale. So use `a.assistant > b.assistant ? 1 : a.assistant < b.assistant ? -1 : 0` or simply `String(a.assistant).localeCompare` no - use default sort. Actually `.sort((a, b) => a.assistant.localeCompare(b.assistant))` is not normal JS string comparison. Use `.sort((a, b) => (a.assistant > b.assistant ? 1 : a.assistant < b.assistant ? -1 : 0))` or just `.sort((a,b) => a.assistant < b.assistant ? -1 : 1)`. The simplest and correct for normal JS comparison is `.sort((a, b) => a.assistant > b.assistant ? 1 : -1)` but that gives 0 if equal? No, if equal it returns -1. That's fine for stability. But better use:\n.sort((a, b) => (a.assistant > b.assistant ? 1 : a.assistant < b.assistant ? -1 : 0))\n\nDo not mutate input: make copies with spread. But the input records might be frozen. We don't need to copy them unless we modify. We won't modify. We just read. But for best run selection, we don't modify. So input array and records remain unchanged.\n\nHowever, when we use Object.freeze in tests, it ensures no mutation.\n\nNow render:\n- validate summaries is array\n- validate each summary has required fields valid\n- Should we validate that summary is an object? Yes, throw TypeError.\n- Positive integer: Number.isInteger(run_count) && run_count > 0\n- Then render rows.\n\nFor escape pipe: value.replaceAll(\"|\", \"\\\\|\")\n\nWait, in JavaScript string, to get literal `\\|` in output, replace with \"\\\\|\" which is backslash-pipe.\n\nThe test expects: `| Open\\|Code | 2 | 95.5 | run\\|2 | 1.250 s |`\nIn a JS string, that's \"| Open\\\\|Code | 2 | 95.5 | run\\\\|2 | 1.250 s |\".\nSo replaceAll(\"|\", \"\\\\|\") works.\n\nHeader: `| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |`\nSeparator: `|---|---:|---:|---|---:|`\n\nNote: \"Best score\" column alignment? It uses `---:` but the value is a number. Actually separator is exactly as given. We don't need to align based on content; just output the exact strings.\n\nFor each row:\n`| ${escapedAssistant} | ${run_count} | ${best_score} | ${escapedBestRunId} | ${seconds} s |`\n\nWait the separator has `---:|---:|---|---:|`. That means:\n- Assistant: left aligned (---)\n- Runs: right aligned (---:)\n- Best score: right aligned (---:)\n- Best run: left aligned (---)\n- Median time: right aligned (---:)\n\nThat matches the header. We just output the separator exactly.\n\nFor empty: header + separator + \"\" + \"_No eligible runs._\" joined by \\n.\n\nNow I need to think about best_score formatting. In test, best_score is 95.5 -> rendered as \"95.5\". Should I use toString? Number.toString gives \"95.5\". If it's an integer like 95, gives \"95\". That's fine.\n\nBut wait: what if best_score is 95.0? It might render as \"95\". The contract doesn't specify formatting for score, just finite number 0-100. The test uses 95.5. I think default number to string is fine.\n\nNow let's write the files.\n\nFor student-tests.mjs, I need at least two meaningful tests. Ideas:\n1. Test that ineligible runs are skipped and invalid ineligible fields don't cause errors. e.g., a run with status \"running\" and invalid score is ignored.\n2. Test tie-breaking by run_id when score and elapsed are tied.\n3. Test median for even number of runs.\n4. Test TypeError for non-array input.\n5. Test TypeError for invalid eligible run fields (e.g., empty run_id, score out of range, negative elapsed).\n6. Test render with multiple rows and pipe escaping.\n7. Test render TypeError for invalid summary fields.\n\nI need at least two. Let me add a few good ones. But I should be careful not to conflict with the committed tests.\n\nTest 1: \"ignores ineligible runs and does not validate their fields\"\n- Input includes runs with status not complete, acceptance fail, comparison_eligible false, with invalid fields.\n- Only eligible runs are used.\n- Verifies median for odd count, etc.\n\nTest 2: \"breaks a best-score and elapsed tie with lexicographically smaller run_id\"\n- Two runs same score and elapsed, different run_id.\n- Best run_id is smaller string.\n\nTest 3: \"throws TypeError for invalid eligible run data\"\n- Run is eligible but has empty run_id, or score >100, or negative elapsed.\n\nTest 4: \"renders multiple summaries in order with pipe escaping\"\n- Two summaries with pipe chars.\n\nTest 5: \"throws TypeError when summaries contains an invalid summary\"\n\nI'll add maybe 3-4 tests to be thorough. But at least two. Let me add 4.\n\nActually, let me think about the contract for summarizeAssistants field names. It says exactly these fields. The test uses deepEqual with objects that have exactly those fields. Good.\n\nOne nuance: score range validation. \"finite number from 0 through 100\" - inclusive. So 0 and 100 are valid.\n\nelapsed_ms \"finite number greater than or equal to zero\" - so 0 is valid. Also Infinity is not finite, -Infinity not finite, NaN not finite.\n\nrun_count \"positive integer\" - so >0 and integer.\n\nNow let's implement.\n\nLet me write the summarize-assistants.mjs file.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":8439,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d","uuid":"21bce3c1-a47f-41f3-b8ec-15e70c8f558d","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:09:24.195Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_4703e21c94d35de9d9920cff","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"functions.Write:7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-oDPFwQ/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/summarize-assistants.mjs","content":"/**\n * Build one comparison summary per assistant from raw benchmark run records.\n */\nexport function summarizeAssistants(runs) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(runs)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"runs must be an array\");\n  }\n\n  const groups = new Map();\n\n  for (const run of runs) {\n    if (\n      run?.status !== \"complete\" ||\n      run?.acceptance_status !== \"pass\" ||\n      run?.comparison_eligible === false\n    ) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    validateEligibleRun(run);\n\n    const assistant = run.assistant;\n    if (!groups.has(assistant)) {\n      groups.set(assistant, []);\n    }\n    groups.get(assistant).push(run);\n  }\n\n  const summaries = [];\n  for (const [assistant, assistantRuns] of groups) {\n    const best = pickBestRun(assistantRuns);\n    const median = medianElapsedMs(assistantRuns);\n\n    summaries.push({\n      assistant,\n      run_count: assistantRuns.length,\n      best_score: best.score,\n      best_run_id: best.run_id,\n      median_elapsed_ms: median,\n    });\n  }\n\n  summaries.sort((a, b) => {\n    if (a.assistant > b.assistant) return 1;\n    if (a.assistant < b.assistant) return -1;\n    return 0;\n  });\n\n  return summaries;\n}\n\nfunction validateEligibleRun(run) {\n  if (!isNonEmptyString(run.run_id)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"eligible run must have a non-empty run_id string\");\n  }\n  if (!isNonEmptyString(run.assistant)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"eligible run must have a non-empty assistant string\");\n  }\n  if (!isFiniteNumber(run.score) || run.score < 0 || run.score > 100) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"eligible run score must be a finite number from 0 to 100\");\n  }\n  if (!isFiniteNumber(run.elapsed_ms) || run.elapsed_ms < 0) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"eligible run elapsed_ms must be a finite number >= 0\");\n  }\n}\n\nfunction isNonEmptyString(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"string\" && value.length > 0;\n}\n\nfunction isFiniteNumber(value) {\n  return typeof value === \"number\" && Number.isFinite(value);\n}\n\nfunction pickBestRun(runs) {\n  return runs.reduce((best, run) => {\n    if (run.score > best.score) return run;\n    if (run.score < best.score) return best;\n    if (run.elapsed_ms < best.elapsed_ms) return run;\n    if (run.elapsed_ms > best.elapsed_ms) return best;\n    return run.run_id < best.run_id ? run : best;\n  });\n}\n\nfunction medianElapsedMs(runs) {\n  const sorted = runs.map((run) => run.elapsed_ms).sort((a, b) => a - b);\n  const mid = Math.floor(sorted.length / 2);\n  if (sorted.length % 2 === 1) {\n    return sorted[mid];\n  }\n  return (sorted[mid - 1] + sorted[mid]) / 2;\n}\n"}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":8439,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d","uuid":"2d9853ff-1908-4606-9096-40ceca003020","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:09:24.204Z"}
