{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2a8d9376fc1823075618d4ef","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now write student-tests.mjs with at least two meaningful tests. Let me add several comprehensive tests.\n\nNeed to import assert and test. Also import the functions.\n\nTests:\n1. \"breaks a three-way tie using score, elapsed time, then run_id\"\n   - Runs: same score, one with lower elapsed wins.\n   - Then: same score and elapsed, lexicographically smaller run_id wins.\n   - Also include a higher score to verify score primary.\n\n2. \"throws TypeError for invalid eligible run fields\"\n   - Eligible run with empty run_id -> TypeError\n   - Could do multiple assertions in one test.\n\n3. \"ignores ineligible runs and skips validation of their fields\"\n   - Ineligible run with missing run_id, NaN score, etc. should be ignored.\n   - Eligible run produces summary.\n\n4. \"renders multiple summaries in supplied order with pipe escaping\"\n   - Two summaries with pipe chars, verify order preserved.\n\n5. \"throws TypeError for invalid summary fields\"\n   - Negative median_elapsed_ms, non-integer run_count, etc.\n\nLet me add 4-5 tests. They need to be real and not placeholders.\n\nActually, I want to be careful with test names and assertions. Let me write them.\n\nAlso I should use Object.freeze? Not necessary but good to show no mutation. I can include frozen arrays.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n```javascript\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { renderComparisonTable } from \"./render-comparison-table.mjs\";\nimport { summarizeAssistants } from \"./summarize-assistants.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"breaks a tie first by lower elapsed time, then by smaller run_id\", () => {\n  const runs = [\n    { run_id: \"z-run\", assistant: \"Model\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 90, elapsed_ms: 800 },\n    { run_id: \"a-run\", assistant: \"Model\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 90, elapsed_ms: 800 },\n    { run_id: \"fast-run\", assistant: \"Model\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 90, elapsed_ms: 700 },\n  ];\n\n  const summary = summarizeAssistants(runs)[0];\n  assert.equal(summary.best_score, 90);\n  assert.equal(summary.best_run_id, \"fast-run\");\n  assert.equal(summary.median_elapsed_ms, 800);\n});\n\ntest(\"ignores ineligible runs and does not validate their fields\", () => {\n  const runs = Object.freeze([\n    Object.freeze({ run_id: \"valid\", assistant: \"A\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 80, elapsed_ms: 100 }),\n    Object.freeze({ status: \"running\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: NaN, elapsed_ms: -1 }),\n    Object.freeze({ run_id: \"fail\", assistant: \"B\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"fail\", score: 200, elapsed_ms: Infinity }),\n    Object.freeze({ run_id: \"excluded\", assistant: \"C\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", comparison_eligible: false, score: \"bad\", elapsed_ms: \"worse\" }),\n  ]);\n\n  const summaries = summarizeAssistants(runs);\n  assert.equal(summaries.length, 1);\n  assert.deepEqual(summaries[0], {\n    assistant: \"A\",\n    run_count: 1,\n    best_score: 80,\n    best_run_id: \"valid\",\n    median_elapsed_ms: 100,\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"throws TypeError for invalid eligible run data\", () => {\n  assert.throws(\n    () => summarizeAssistants([{ run_id: \"\", assistant: \"A\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 50, elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => summarizeAssistants([{ run_id: \"r\", assistant: \"\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 50, elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => summarizeAssistants([{ run_id: \"r\", assistant: \"A\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 101, elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => summarizeAssistants([{ run_id: \"r\", assistant: \"A\", status: \"complete\", acceptance_status: \"pass\", score: 50, elapsed_ms: -1 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"renders summaries in the supplied order and escapes pipes\", () => {\n  const summaries = [\n    { assistant: \"A|B\", run_count: 1, best_score: 88, best_run_id: \"r1\", median_elapsed_ms: 500 },\n    { assistant: \"C\", run_count: 2, best_score: 92.5, best_run_id: \"r|2\", median_elapsed_ms: 1_750 },\n  ];\n\n  assert.equal(\n    renderComparisonTable(summaries),\n    [\n      \"| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |\",\n      \"|---|---:|---:|---|---:|\",\n      \"| A\\\\|B | 1 | 88 | r1 | 0.500 s |\",\n      \"| C | 2 | 92.5 | r\\\\|2 | 1.750 s |\",\n    ].join(\"\\n\"),\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"throws TypeError for invalid summary fields\", () => {\n  assert.throws(\n    () => renderComparisonTable([{ assistant: \"\", run_count: 1, best_score: 50, best_run_id: \"r\", median_elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => renderComparisonTable([{ assistant: \"A\", run_count: 0, best_score: 50, best_run_id: \"r\", median_elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => renderComparisonTable([{ assistant: \"A\", run_count: 1, best_score: 101, best_run_id: \"r\", median_elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => renderComparisonTable([{ assistant: \"A\", run_count: 1, best_score: 50, best_run_id: \"\", median_elapsed_ms: 10 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n  assert.throws(\n    () => renderComparisonTable([{ assistant: \"A\", run_count: 1, best_score: 50, best_run_id: \"r\", median_elapsed_ms: -1 }]),\n    TypeError,\n  );\n});\n```\n\nWait, in test 1, median of [800, 800, 700] sorted [700, 800, 800] -> median 800. Good. run_count 3. best is fast-run. Good.\n\nIn test 2, note that the second ineligible run has no run_id and no assistant. Accessing `run?.status` is \"running\" so it's skipped before validation. The third is fail. The fourth has comparison_eligible false. Good.\n\nNow, one concern: the eligible run validation function uses optional chaining `run?.status`. But if run is null or undefined, `run?.status` is undefined, which is not \"complete\", so it's skipped. Good.\n\nBut what if `run` is not an object? The contract doesn't say we need to throw TypeError for non-object elements. It just says check eligibility. If run is a primitive, `run?.status` is undefined, so it's ineligible. That's acceptable. The contract doesn't require validating ineligible runs. However, if run is null, accessing other fields won't happen. Good.\n\nWait: my eligible check uses `run?.comparison_eligible === false`. If run is a primitive, `run?.comparison_eligible` is undefined, so not false. If status is not \"complete\" or acceptance not \"pass\", it skips. Good.\n\nBut what if an object has `status: \"complete\"`, `acceptance_status: \"pass\"`, and no `comparison_eligible` - then eligible. Good.\n\nNow let me think about whether I need to validate `run_id` and `assistant` non-empty strings. I do.\n\nEdge case: score exactly 0 or 100 is valid. Good.\n\nEdge case: elapsed_ms exactly 0 is valid. Good.\n\nNow write student-tests.mjs.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":12280,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d","uuid":"c5a8584e-2d59-4abd-87b7-8dfe72f9cd43","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:09:46.018Z"}
