{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_6f00e5208156fc7e82c7e91a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 9 tests pass. Now I need to provide a final response summarizing the design, edge cases covered, and verification result.\n\nLet me also think about whether there are any other verification commands I should run. The prompt says \"Run: node --test ...\" which I did. It also mentions standard commands but those are general. The task specifically asks to run that command.\n\nI should also consider if the implementation is correct in all aspects. Let me double-check one thing: the committed test uses `Object.freeze` on the input array and objects, and my implementation doesn't mutate them - it just iterates. Good.\n\nAnother thing: in `summarize-assistants.mjs`, I use optional chaining `run?.status`. This is fine. But I should think about whether we should explicitly check if run is an object. The contract doesn't require it. Ineligible runs can be primitives and are skipped. Good.\n\nOne more nuance: the contract says \"Group eligible runs by the exact, case-sensitive assistant value.\" My Map key is the string. Good.\n\n\"Sort the returned summaries by assistant using normal JavaScript string comparison.\" I used `>` and `<` comparison. Good.\n\n\"Return one object per assistant with exactly these fields\" - I create new objects with only those fields. Good.\n\n\"Do not mutate the input array or its records.\" - I don't. Good.\n\n\"Median time uses all eligible runs for the assistant after a numeric sort. For an even count, average the two middle values.\" - I use numeric sort, average. Good.\n\nFor render: \"Preserve the supplied summary order.\" - I iterate in order. Good.\n\n\"Return this exact Markdown header\" - exact. Good.\n\n\"Render median milliseconds as seconds with exactly three decimal places.\" - toFixed(3). Good.\n\n\"Escape | in assistant names and run IDs as \\|.\" - replaceAll. Good.\n\n\"For an empty array, render the two header lines, a blank line, and _No eligible runs._.\" - Done. Good.\n\n\"Throw TypeError when summaries is not an array or a summary has invalid fields.\" - Done. Good.\n\nNow the final response.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":15842,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d","uuid":"44e2c296-ab62-4f22-9f70-e22bc71fbf52","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:09:50.607Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_6f00e5208156fc7e82c7e91a","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"kimi-k2.7-code","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implemented the comparison-summary feature and added tests. All 9 tests pass.\n\n### Design summary\n\n**`summarize-assistants.mjs`**\n- Rejects non-array input with a `TypeError`.\n- Skips runs unless `status === \"complete\"`, `acceptance_status === \"pass\"`, and `comparison_eligible !== false` (so `true`, absent, or `undefined` all count as eligible).\n- Validates only eligible runs: `run_id` and `assistant` must be non-empty strings; `score` must be finite and in `[0, 100]`; `elapsed_ms` must be finite and `>= 0`. Ineligible runs with garbage fields are ignored.\n- Groups by exact, case-sensitive `assistant`, picks the best run by highest score → lowest elapsed → lexicographically smallest `run_id`, and computes the median `elapsed_ms` from all eligible runs for that assistant.\n- Returns new summary objects with exactly the required fields, sorted by `assistant` using normal JS string comparison. The input array and records are never mutated.\n\n**`render-comparison-table.mjs`**\n- Rejects non-array input and invalid summary objects with a `TypeError`.\n- Validates `assistant`/`best_run_id` are non-empty strings, `run_count` is a positive integer, `best_score` is finite in `[0, 100]`, and `median_elapsed_ms` is finite and `>= 0`.\n- Preserves summary order and emits the exact Markdown header/separator.\n- Converts median milliseconds to seconds with `toFixed(3)` and escapes `|` as `\\|`.\n- Empty input renders the header, a blank line, and `_No eligible runs._`.\n\n### Added `student-tests.mjs` edge cases\n\n1. **Tie-breaking:** same score ties are broken by lower elapsed time, then by lexicographically smaller `run_id`.\n2. **Ineligible run tolerance:** runs that are incomplete, failed, or explicitly `comparison_eligible: false` are skipped, even when their fields would fail eligible-run validation.\n3. **Eligible-run validation:** empty strings, out-of-range scores, and negative elapsed times throw `TypeError`.\n4. **Render ordering and escaping:** multiple summaries keep their input order and `|` characters in assistant names/run IDs are escaped.\n5. **Render validation:** empty strings, non-positive run counts, out-of-range scores, and negative median times throw `TypeError`.\n\n### Verification result\n\n```text\nnode --test benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs\n```\n\nResult: **9 passed, 0 failed**."}],"usage":{"input_tokens":15842,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f942b9e-6087-4a0e-a1ac-354bc45f970d","uuid":"348095e7-9bee-4660-81b3-07f4f5fcb8e7","timestamp":"2026-08-23T00:09:53.418Z"}
